Subject: [PATCH] app_server: pick the default UI scale from the display's pixel density

When no font sizes have been chosen, app_server enlarges the default fonts
(and with them controls, window borders, icons and the cursor, which all
scale by the font size) on large screens. It decided by resolution alone:
x1.5 above 1920x1080, x2 above 3840x2160. Resolution says nothing about
density: a 27" 2560x1440 monitor (109 dpi) got x1.5 and crowded its own
screen, a 13" 2560x1600 laptop panel (227 dpi) got x1.5 too and stayed
tiny, and a 15" 3840x2160 panel (282 dpi) got x1.5 because the test was
">", not ">=".

Use the size the display reports in its EDID (monitor_info width/height,
in cm) when there is one: scale = dpi / 110, in quarter steps between 1
and 3. Displays without EDID keep the resolution rule (now inclusive of
3840x2160). The decision is logged to the syslog.

Ported from renkuos-apps/renku-retina (patch 0001), this port's own
sibling project that packages this as rretina for pkgman install after
boot. Folding it into arm64-patch bakes it into the image itself, so
the correct scale is already picked by app_server's own first
Desktop::Init() -- during the live ISO boot, before Installer ever
opens, not only after a later pkgman install. Applies cleanly as-is to
this port's pinned commit.

diff -ru a/src/servers/app/Desktop.cpp b/src/servers/app/Desktop.cpp
--- a/src/servers/app/Desktop.cpp	2026-10-09 23:08:39
+++ b/src/servers/app/Desktop.cpp	2026-10-09 23:11:38
@@ -21,10 +21,13 @@
 
 #include "Desktop.h"
 
+#include <math.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <syslog.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
+
 #include <Debug.h>
 #include <debugger.h>
 #include <DirectWindow.h>
@@ -486,6 +489,49 @@
 
 /*!	This method is allowed to throw exceptions.
 */
+/*!	The factor the default fonts - and with them everything that scales by
+	the font size: controls, window borders, icons, the cursor - are scaled by
+	when the user has not chosen font sizes. It follows the display's pixel
+	density when the display tells its size (EDID), in steps of a quarter
+	between 1 and 3: 110 dpi is still comfortable at the unscaled 12 pt, so a
+	27" 2560x1440 panel (109 dpi) stays at 1, a 13" 2560x1600 one (227 dpi)
+	gets 2, and a 15" 3840x2160 one (282 dpi) 2.5. Displays without EDID (a
+	firmware frame buffer) fall back to the resolution alone.
+*/
+/*static*/ float
+Desktop::_AutomaticUIScale(Screen* screen)
+{
+	display_mode mode;
+	screen->GetMode(mode);
+	if (mode.virtual_width == 0)
+		return 1.0f;
+
+	float scale;
+	monitor_info info;
+	if (screen->GetMonitorInfo(info) == B_OK && info.width >= 10.0f
+		&& info.width < 400.0f && info.height >= 5.0f) {
+		// EDID sizes are in cm; anything outside that range is an aspect
+		// ratio, a projector, or garbage
+		float dpi = mode.virtual_width / (info.width / 2.54f);
+		scale = roundf(dpi / 110.0f * 4.0f) / 4.0f;
+		syslog(LOG_INFO, "app_server: %ux%u on a %.0fx%.0f cm display, "
+			"%.0f dpi: UI scale %.2f\n", mode.virtual_width,
+			mode.virtual_height, info.width, info.height, dpi, scale);
+	} else {
+		if (mode.virtual_width >= 3840 && mode.virtual_height >= 2160)
+			scale = 2.0f;
+		else if (mode.virtual_width > 1920 && mode.virtual_height > 1080)
+			scale = 1.5f;
+		else
+			scale = 1.0f;
+		syslog(LOG_INFO, "app_server: %ux%u, display size unknown: "
+			"UI scale %.2f\n", mode.virtual_width, mode.virtual_height, scale);
+	}
+
+	return std::max(1.0f, std::min(scale, 3.0f));
+}
+
+
 status_t
 Desktop::Init()
 {
@@ -546,15 +592,8 @@
 		float fontSize = fSettings->DefaultPlainFont().Size();
 		gScreenManager->Lock();
 		Screen* screen = gScreenManager->ScreenAt(0);
-		if (screen != NULL) {
-			display_mode mode;
-			screen->GetMode(mode);
-
-			if (mode.virtual_width > 3840 && mode.virtual_height > 2160)
-				fontSize *= 2.0f;
-			else if (mode.virtual_width > 1920 && mode.virtual_height > 1080)
-				fontSize *= 1.5f;
-		}
+		if (screen != NULL)
+			fontSize *= _AutomaticUIScale(screen);
 		gScreenManager->Unlock();
 
 		// modify settings without saving them
diff -ru a/src/servers/app/Desktop.h b/src/servers/app/Desktop.h
--- a/src/servers/app/Desktop.h	2026-10-09 23:08:39
+++ b/src/servers/app/Desktop.h	2026-10-09 23:09:10
@@ -276,6 +276,7 @@
 
 			void				_FlushPendingColors();
 
+	static	float				_AutomaticUIScale(Screen* screen);
 			void				_LaunchInputServer();
 			void				_GetLooperName(char* name, size_t size);
 			void				_PrepareQuit();
